  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A beluga whale showed up wearing a harness labelled St Petersburg. Off Hammerfest, northern Norway, April 2019. It came straight up to the fishing boats.",
        "visual_query": "arctic norway fishing harbour coast",
        "visual_fallback": "arctic harbour"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The harness was tight-fitting, with a mount for a GoPro and no camera in it. The clasp read Equipment St Petersburg.",
        "visual_query": "beluga whale underwater arctic water",
        "visual_fallback": "beluga whale"
      },
      {
        "narration": "He played fetch. He brought a kayaker's dropped camera back up off the harbour floor. He answered hand signals. So who trained him?",
        "visual_query": "norwegian fjord boat water surface",
        "visual_fallback": "fjord water"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Norway named him Hvaldimir, from hval, whale, plus Vladimir. Russia never confirmed a thing, and one Russian military commentator would not rule out a navy escape.",
        "visual_query": "cold northern sea ice coastline",
        "visual_fallback": "northern sea"
      },
      {
        "narration": "He was found dead near Stavanger in August 2024. No bullets: the post-mortem pointed at infection from a stick lodged in his mouth. Who sent him out is still unanswered.",
        "visual_query": "stavanger norway harbour water dusk",
        "visual_fallback": "harbour dusk"
      }
    ],
